March 9, 2026

Dear Supporter,

Join us on Tuesday, March 10th for a workshop designed
specifically for Parent Plus Loan holders. With critical
deadlines at the end of the month and changes coming to the
entire student loan program, you won't want to miss out!

RSVP: PARENT PLUS LOAN WORKSHOP, MARCH 10TH AT 7 PM ET / 4 PM
PT 
( https://redirect.moveon.org/ss/c/u001.4ldQ0ramg-FlrQgepO-djAJioPxHdIxQoZtK1K37cjilRM3w5paR5JqQw12i6O-1Qovkx91FkdfJ5c3k-WwTWqM-f1BJw-JH_w2XP0zFEkk/4ot/t1Q0NEcuQKmQMRYzUaR0Gg/t0/h001.9rdn6VaYByi7ldSsqNDbU_M24Iw1yuW1Qn64JO7GXus )


You can’t afford to miss out on what we will be covering:

- Upcoming Parent Plus Loan deadlines,

- Changes to repayment plan options,

- Loan limits for future Parent Plus Loans,

- Important notes on loan consolidation, and much more!

These changes are difficult to navigate alone, so we are here to
provide the latest updates, guidance, and answer your questions.

In addition to these changes, countless Parent Plus borrowers may
lose access to Income Driven Repayment plans if their loans are
not consolidated by July 1st. Take action now by adding your name
to demand that the Department of Education process these
applications in time, and it honors timely applications. 
( https://redirect.moveon.org/ss/c/u001.3mymh0y1wrIodqOdyCoj4duIb_1BmaUlZZDQ-y9VvTr04DlX4q897x3KCspYo5g09uitxv6VKJP_8R-aicosLPWqPoj-Accod5tG71O7BrCfj6I1xreYrAtlmHoKfvW7/4ot/t1Q0NEcuQKmQMRYzUaR0Gg/t1/h001.PrMbF2C709BVxnp2H2mBYM9XTPQ6Ba6MneqS3DGzehM )


Secure your spot for our workshop before it fills up! 
( https://redirect.moveon.org/ss/c/u001.4ldQ0ramg-FlrQgepO-djAJioPxHdIxQoZtK1K37cjilRM3w5paR5JqQw12i6O-1Qovkx91FkdfJ5c3k-WwTWqM-f1BJw-JH_w2XP0zFEkk/4ot/t1Q0NEcuQKmQMRYzUaR0Gg/t2/h001.P11A0F1hwT374CvjohJY9oIhwPsVqrkGTtJOFA-DjzI )
 We hope to see you there, and encourage you to invite a friend
or two! As always, we will continue to support you as we navigate
the major overhaul of the student loan system together.

In Community,

Team SDCC

Student Debt Crisis Center (SDCC) is a 501(c)(3) nonprofit
that centers the needs and voices of borrowers, and partners with
allies, to impact public policy and end the student debt crisis.
We are a people-powered movement representing over 2 million
supporters.

Donations to SDCC are tax deductible to the full extent of the
law. 
( https://redirect.moveon.org/ss/c/u001.OU9JUeVLcHljNKW5B6v_o9iHIBxD8RohwQ0M_S3p_D_yCMxTb5JZNpoBtAntnYIJrKBh25rpi8nAqaBHWI7yoKcZ2lrFhcvUlDNe2ycR9TA/4ot/t1Q0NEcuQKmQMRYzUaR0Gg/t3/h001.ho64EnpGt1uvjD9sQazTG_HEJGdl-94BFPc2V7nLO14 )

