March 5, 2026

Dear Supporter,

On Friday, February 27th a judge dismissed a settlement that
aimed to eliminate the SAVE plan, and yesterday, a judge denied
the attempt to appeal the dismissal. This means that the SAVE
plan is live, leaving the Department of Education with no reason
to not allow borrowers to access SAVE and its benefits, including
loan forgiveness. We don’t know how long the SAVE plan will stick
around, so now we need your help to save it.

ADD YOUR NAME TO SAVE THE SAVE PLAN 
( https://redirect.moveon.org/ss/c/u001.3mymh0y1wrIodqOdyCoj4duIb_1BmaUlZZDQ-y9VvTpdshzikI9UCrY8T9m4jZJjsHvBiqcfLt1hvRSCcIbYlA/4oq/0tlmi_-TR3Sm6Rj2pnmgYQ/t0/h001.3XtqdEIETSP-aYDrykcIgqtw9OOJ6YrxqIL37RgEhqs )

This is an important moment to make our voices heard and to
save the SAVE plan. A lot of uncertainty remains, and we don’t
know what will happen, but we cannot afford to miss out on this
chance to help millions of Americans enrolled in a plan that
offered the lowest monthly payments, shortened repayment terms
for smaller balances, and capped interest– something that
frustrates so many of us. The positive impact of the SAVE plan is
immeasurable.

If you are enrolled in SAVE, we need to hear from you. If you had
a zero dollar payment or originally had a balance lower than
$12,000 and have been in repayment for more than 10 years, it is
especially important that you fill out this form 
( https://redirect.moveon.org/ss/c/u001.fEjkuMNtIlzPuqQTIoOJUoan4ICRiBrEtafv_-Bq-5qCszuG-F0QLQx8xkHqC3EGUMUbAmbtPBBJU0jaBTckJHFcadpsfqg6qiAswzJqgvgaHP21gXe8FFbUdIdWsSy4CLRYY1EPGD0RTKiIbXaAvpTWwg_0Xp9oOkMS7o-21bs/4oq/0tlmi_-TR3Sm6Rj2pnmgYQ/t1/h001.Iz-wrnsJAiAlRHocHy9pTDS5e_2s0rCX55CYtE1aeQk )
.

We don’t know whether we’ll succeed in saving SAVE, but we owe it
to ourselves to give it a try. Take a moment to add your name and
put pressure on the Department of Education to protect the
well-being of Americans with student loan debt. 
( https://redirect.moveon.org/ss/c/u001.3mymh0y1wrIodqOdyCoj4duIb_1BmaUlZZDQ-y9VvTpdshzikI9UCrY8T9m4jZJjsHvBiqcfLt1hvRSCcIbYlA/4oq/0tlmi_-TR3Sm6Rj2pnmgYQ/t2/h001.Gib2NsxRuLeK_yZaonnBJrTJhYTS_aW9WSf_M-NQJTc ) Thank
you again for your support.

Together, we will end the student debt crisis,

Team SDCC

Student Debt Crisis Center (SDCC) is a 501(c)(3) nonprofit
that centers the needs and voices of borrowers, and partners with
allies, to impact public policy and end the student debt crisis.
We are a people-powered movement representing over 2 million
supporters.

Donations to SDCC are tax deductible to the full extent of the
law. 
( https://redirect.moveon.org/ss/c/u001.OU9JUeVLcHljNKW5B6v_o9iHIBxD8RohwQ0M_S3p_D_yCMxTb5JZNpoBtAntnYIJrKBh25rpi8nAqaBHWI7yoKcZ2lrFhcvUlDNe2ycR9TA/4oq/0tlmi_-TR3Sm6Rj2pnmgYQ/t3/h001.hBYF9a0gR4GRl9sC29060NMMDioIaHcWJATCVp3vH0o )

