March 3, 2026

Dear Supporter,

On Friday, January 27th, the courts dismissed the settlement that
sought to end the SAVE Plan - a move that keeps this vital
program alive - for now. This decision means the SAVE Plan is
still in place, but could soon come to an end in the coming weeks
or months.

While the settlement was dismissed, our fight is far from over.

BORROWERS DESERVE CLARITY: PROCESS ALL APPLICATIONS NOW 
( https://redirect.moveon.org/ss/c/u001.3mymh0y1wrIodqOdyCoj4duIb_1BmaUlZZDQ-y9VvTr04DlX4q897x3KCspYo5g0Y5Qpki8fDSyyjYds_e6rxKDVpykZmEfQw3ua2oLCDuK8eYFwCf2-W9969CjlrLXMm6In7X5wOE7a9K31KRvYgOVbugUd5XBbA4xAx2ib-eXXB3VpL9KD0LzonjNDWNx8/4on/ri7bMenMTcuDxvTfaRe82A/t0/h001.06328ohmDomIMWyFOUyt4bkb460ntIyYxP9E91PhJy4 )


The Department of Education (ED) has made it clear that it
still intends to move forward with terminating the SAVE Plan and
implementing a major overhaul to the student loan repayment
system. At the same time, millions of borrowers’ applications
remain stuck in limbo. For all student loan borrowers and their
families who depend on vital Income-Driven Repayment (IDR) Plans
and Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF), it is of utmost
importance that the administrative delays currently preventing
borrowers from accessing these programs be immediately resolved.

If the Department of Education is to truly do its job of serving
American families, it must act promptly by immediately processing
the backlog of applications and providing borrowers with the
clarity they deserve. Keeping applications frozen only deepens
confusion, financial strain, and emotional stress as borrowers
prepare for the phase out of the SAVE plan.

Now is the moment to make our voices heard. Add your name and
demand that these applications be immediately processed 
( https://redirect.moveon.org/ss/c/u001.3mymh0y1wrIodqOdyCoj4duIb_1BmaUlZZDQ-y9VvTr04DlX4q897x3KCspYo5g0Y5Qpki8fDSyyjYds_e6rxKDVpykZmEfQw3ua2oLCDuK8eYFwCf2-W9969CjlrLXMm6In7X5wOE7a9K31KRvYgOVbugUd5XBbA4xAx2ib-eUi-ZyeRAZ8JK9KGc7U87Ia/4on/ri7bMenMTcuDxvTfaRe82A/t1/h001.tjylx1Mhg6dbsA3LqU1Y9qI3sAv9uSBcdhln0c-GMsM )
.

We’re once again in a state of unknown, but we’re dedicated to
bringing you the most up-to-date information on the SAVE plan and
everything else in the student debt space.

Team SDCC

Student Debt Crisis Center (SDCC) is a 501(c)(3) nonprofit
that centers the needs and voices of borrowers, and partners with
allies, to impact public policy and end the student debt crisis.
We are a people-powered movement representing over 2 million
