February 27, 2026

Dear Supporter,

We have 5 days to speak out against the major student loan
overhaul set to take effect in July. The public comment period
closes on March 2, and we need as many people as possible to make
their voices heard. Whether you have student debt or care about
someone planning to attend college in the years ahead, these
changes will affect all of us. It only takes a few minutes to
submit a comment. Add your voice before the deadline.

CLICK HERE TO SUBMIT YOUR COMMENT OPPOSING THE HARMFUL
STUDENT LOAN OVERHAUL 
( https://redirect.moveon.org/ss/c/u001.3mymh0y1wrIodqOdyCoj4duIb_1BmaUlZZDQ-y9VvTrvw39HWc_LjMafLgXGMd0ed_AuZFrN1K8nF3l0vcpJBxGXrqdinhfSUpk2eVbHbwwCfQ-vx9WqEZDdYNUni_79LvJm84bK4iBQnHue0Z-rPC9HbQm159BwXNnAIHJ-peX6w-lRbSQW7yciCq9Fg479/4ol/Uqss5QstRw6X9aNUNu0zfQ/t0/h001.xDyRuHoN53f9PyRoHvi2h3Mx6jl-7wgIScHbZ2y8Iwg )


If the final rule is approved as is, this is what the student
loan system will look like moving forward:

- Expensive repayment plans with longer repayment periods (up to
30 years).

- Zero Income-Driven Repayment (IDR) options for new Parent PLUS
loans.

- Fewer IDR Plans (PAYE & ICR are phasing out).

- Federal lending limits.

- Reduced protections and relief for borrowers.

- An inaccessible higher education system.

- Increased rates of default and delinquency.

- A student loan system that does not value or put the needs of
borrowers first.

We cannot afford to miss out on this opportunity to voice our
collective opposition to these incoming changes. This final rule
would worsen the $1.7 trillion crisis while harming millions of
Americans and their families. This is the complete opposite of
the American dream.

Together, our voices can make a difference when so much is at
stake. Your public comment can help highlight the real-life
impact of these changes 
( https://redirect.moveon.org/ss/c/u001.3mymh0y1wrIodqOdyCoj4duIb_1BmaUlZZDQ-y9VvTrvw39HWc_LjMafLgXGMd0ed_AuZFrN1K8nF3l0vcpJBxGXrqdinhfSUpk2eVbHbwwCfQ-vx9WqEZDdYNUni_79LvJm84bK4iBQnHue0Z-rPC9HbQm159BwXNnAIHJ-peX6w-lRbSQW7yciCq9Fg479/4ol/Uqss5QstRw6X9aNUNu0zfQ/t1/h001.OFMgIl-Tw3ySyPLF0TC9hqi2aiX78j0U3eNeItjUQ4Y )
. We must do everything possible to stop this from being
implemented. As always, thank you for standing with us.

In Solidarity,

Team SDCC

